# Data Center Deployment Visualizer — Cursor Rules

## Stack

- React, TypeScript, Vite, Zustand, Zod
- Cytoscape.js with Dagre (default), Grid, AVSDF, Concentric, Circle, Breadth-first, and Cose
- MUI primitives customized with Tailwind CSS
- Phosphor Icons via direct imports
- Vitest, React Testing Library, Cypress, MSW, ESLint, and Prettier

## Architecture

- Keep domain logic framework-independent and validate external data with Zod.
- Use feature-oriented modules under `src/features`.
- Keep normalized graph state in Zustand with narrow selectors.
- Keep imperative Cytoscape code inside `GraphCanvas`.
- Prefer pure functions, explicit types, and small composable components.

## UI rules

- Use existing Tailwind tokens and shared UI components.
- Use Phosphor icons instead of text glyphs or improvised SVGs.
- Static cards must not have hover effects implying clickability.
- Interactive controls need accessible labels and keyboard support.
- Bound and search long menus; confirm destructive actions.
- Keep toast surfaces neutral; use icon/accent color for state.
- Preserve responsive behavior from mobile through large monitors.

## Performance rules

- Avoid full graph relayouts for status/progress-only updates.
- Use `cy.batch()` for graph mutations and limit labels in dense views.
- Keep dataset previews at 100/500/1,000 unless measured requirements change.
- For production scale, cluster by rack/site and expand on demand.
- Profile memory, layout time, and pan/zoom responsiveness before adding workers.

## Verification

Run before completing changes:

```text
npm run format:check
npm run typecheck
npm run lint
npm test -- --run
npm run build
```

Update relevant docs when architecture, UX behavior, data scale, or testing
responsibilities change.
